From: lfdevs <lfdevs@lfdevs.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 22:37:20 +0800
Subject: backends/anland: Detach audio before closing transport fds

Invoke the fallback callback before releasing consumer resources so the PipeWire audio loop source is removed while its borrowed socket fd is still valid.

Closing the fd first could race with the audio loop and leave it dispatching a stale source during consumer disconnects. The observed failures jumped to invalid callback addresses from the anland-audio thread.
---
 src/backends/anland/anland_backend.cpp | 10 ++++++----
 src/backends/anland/display_producer.c |  7 +++++--
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/anland/anland_backend.cpp b/src/backends/anland/anland_backend.cpp
index 370c6b7..ff9e731 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_backend.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_backend.cpp
@@ -448,8 +448,9 @@ void AnlandBackend::enterFallback()
 
     teardownNotifiers();
 
-    // Renderer is stopped: drop the imported dmabuf set now that the producer's fds
-    // are gone. The layer is null at startup (no GL backend attached yet).
+    // Renderer is stopped: drop the imported dmabuf set before the transport closes
+    // its fds when this callback returns. The layer is null at startup (no GL backend
+    // attached yet).
     if (AnlandEglLayer *layer = m_outputs[0]->eglLayer()) {
         layer->releaseBuffers();
     }
@@ -457,8 +458,9 @@ void AnlandBackend::enterFallback()
     m_consumerReady = false;
     m_inFallback = true;
 
-    // Detach the audio socket: the streams keep running (capture drops its PCM, the
-    // mic Source feeds silence) so PipeWire never perceives the disconnect.
+    // Detach the audio socket before the transport closes the borrowed fd. The streams
+    // keep running (capture drops its PCM, the mic Source feeds silence), so PipeWire
+    // never perceives the disconnect.
     anland_audio_set_fd(-1);
 
     // The consumer's camera fds are now dead: stop recording, destroy the virtual
diff --git a/src/backends/anland/display_producer.c b/src/backends/anland/display_producer.c
index a9deafd..8d0e896 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/display_producer.c
+++ b/src/backends/anland/display_producer.c
@@ -67,10 +67,13 @@ static void enter_fallback(display_ctx *ctx)
         return;
     ctx->fallback = true;
 
-    release_consumer_resources(ctx);
-
+    /* Let the backend detach users of borrowed fds (notably PipeWire's audio
+     * loop source) before those fds are closed below. Destroying a loop source
+     * after its fd has already been closed can leave a stale dispatch entry. */
     if (ctx->fallback_cb)
         ctx->fallback_cb(ctx->fallback_userdata);
+
+    release_consumer_resources(ctx);
 }
 
